# Test fixtures must be BYTE-STABLE across platforms. Several checks here assert
# on exact bytes — a floors mutation locates a literal sentence, and the memory
# index parses a frontmatter fence — so a checkout that rewrites line endings
# changes the thing under test and the failure reads as a logic fault rather
# than a checkout one. Found by CI on its first Windows run.
#
# CRLF TOLERANCE IS A SEPARATE QUESTION AND IS NOT ANSWERED HERE. This governs
# THIS repo's own files. Handling a CRLF file supplied by a USER is the tool's
# job, and is covered by a unit test rather than by a checkout setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
